diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 666ae39d..553abfa7 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -31,9 +31,24 @@ All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file. For info on
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- `Rack::Directory` listings now open with a `<!DOCTYPE html>` and an `<html lang="en">` element, so a browser renders them in standards mode and a screen reader has a language to announce. `Rack::ShowStatus` and `Rack::ShowExceptions` already emitted both.
+- `Rack::QueryParser` and `Rack::MediaType.split` now raise `ArgumentError` for an empty separator instead of letting the empty character class they build surface as a bare `RegexpError`. `Rack::MediaType.split` previously disagreed with itself on this input, refusing it on the quote-free path while returning the whole header on the quoted one.
 - `Rack::Multipart::UploadedFile` now delegates keyword arguments to the wrapped tempfile. Calls such as `uploaded_file.readlines(chomp: true)` raised `TypeError` on Ruby 3.0+. ([#2481](https://github.com/rack/rack/issues/2481), [#2499](https://github.com/rack/rack/pull/2499), [@SeanLF](https://github.com/SeanLF))
 - Multipart parser: limit MIME header size check to the unread buffer region to avoid false `multipart mime part header too large` errors when previously read data accumulates in the scan buffer. ([#2392](https://github.com/rack/rack/pull/2392), [@alpaca-tc](https://github.com/alpaca-tc), [@willnet](https://github.com/willnet), [@krororo](https://github.com/krororo))
 - Multipart parser: add nil guards to prevent `NoMethodError` crashes when handling `Content-Disposition` without parameters and `Content-Type` parameters without '='. ([@haruki0409](https://github.com/haruki0409))
+- Multipart parser: `multipart_file_limit` and `multipart_total_part_limit` are now inclusive bounds, as documented. A request carrying exactly the configured number of parts is accepted; previously it was rejected and only `limit - 1` parts were admitted.
+- `Rack::Multipart.build_multipart` now handles arrays of scalars, which previously raised `NoMethodError`, and no longer drops parts that share a name, so an array of hashes round trips through the parser with every record intact.
+- `Rack::MediaType.params` no longer raises `NoMethodError` on a content type carrying an empty parameter segment, such as `text/plain;;charset=utf-8`, which reached applications through `Rack::Request#media_type_params` and `#content_charset`.
+- `Rack::MediaType.params` and `Rack::MediaType.type` honour quoted parameter values, so a separator inside quotes no longer splits the parameter list. `Rack::MediaType::SPLIT_PATTERN` is replaced by `Rack::MediaType.split`.
+- The multipart boundary parameter may be a quoted string containing a comma, which RFC 2046 allows; previously such a boundary was truncated at the comma and the request failed with `EmptyContentError`.
+- `Rack::Utils.q_values` and `Rack::Request#accept_encoding`/`#accept_language` honour quoted parameter values, so a comma or semicolon inside quotes no longer produces a spurious extra entry; `q_values` now skips empty entries instead of returning `[nil, 1.0]` for them.
+- The multipart parser no longer reads a part's `charset` out of the inside of a quoted parameter value, which could force a part body to an unrelated encoding and fail the request.
+- `Rack::QueryParser#new_depth_limit` carries `bytesize_limit` and `params_limit` across to the derived parser instead of resetting them to the defaults, and `Rack::Utils.param_depth_limit=` installs the result frozen, so setting a depth limit no longer discards a configured limit or costs Ractor shareability.
+- A query separator is now treated as a literal set of characters. Previously it was interpolated into a regular expression character class unescaped, so `"^"` raised a bare `RegexpError`, `"]"` and a repeated character emitted Ruby warnings, and `"a-z"` was silently read as a character range.
+- `Rack::Reloader.new(app, nil)` now builds a reloader that never reloads, which is what `Reloader#call`'s own `if @cooldown` guard implies. Previously the constructor computed `Time.now - cooldown` before that guard could apply and raised `TypeError` at boot.
+- Media type and Accept header parsing takes a plain split when the header contains no double quote, so honouring quoted parameter values costs the character scanner only on headers that actually carry one.
+- `Rack::MediaType.type` and `.params` handle a separator-only `Content-Type` such as `;` without raising, returning `""` and `{}` as they always did; `Rack::Request#media_type`, `#form_data?`, `#parseable_data?` and `#POST` are reachable with such a header.
+- The multipart parser no longer raises `NoMethodError` on a part whose `Content-Type` ends in a separator, such as `text/plain;`.
 
